speechtext:
That a sum not exceeding $10,358,774,745.49 being the aggregate of:
(a)	three-twelfths of the total of the amounts of the Items set forth in the Estimates for the fiscal year ending March 31, 1985, laid before the House of Commons on Tuesday, February 21, 1984, $9,287,918,349.75;
(b)	an additional eight-twelfths of the total amount of Communications Item 35, Public Works Items 65 and 75, Transport Item 25 and Treasury Board Item 10 (Schedule A) of the said Estimates $12,272,733.33;
(c)	an additional six-twelfths of the total amount of Treasury Board Item 5 (Schedule B) of the said Estimates $157,500,000;
(d)	an additional three-twelfths of the total amount of Indian Affairs and Northern Development Item 15, Transport Items 20, 35, L60 and LI 15 (Schedule C) of the said Estimates $226,445,000;
(p) an additional two-twelfths of the total amount of Communications Item 5, Environment Items 15 and 30, Public Works Items 20, 30, 70 and 80, Regional Industrial Expansion Item 35, Secretary of State Item 30 and Transport Item 90 (Schedule D) of the said Estimates $118,331,748.83;
Supply
if) an additional one-twelfth of the total amount of Agriculture Item 15, Communications Item 45, Consumer and Corporate Affairs Items 1 and 5, Employment and Immigration Item 15, Energy, Mines and Resources Item 1, Environment Items 1 and 20, External Affairs Items 5 and 40, Indian Affairs and Northern Development Items 30, 35 and 40, Labour Item 5, National Health and Welfare Items 10 and 45, Public Works Item 10, Secretary of State Item 10, Solicitor General Item 1, Supply and Services Item 1, Transport Items 65 and 100, Veterans Affairs Items 25 and 30 (Schedule E) of the said Estimates $555,806,877.58;
be granted to Her Majesty on account of the fiscal year ending March 31, 1985.
